 "structural_change": "HBM-HCBANK10 10-21 cbrw5m: structural successor of hbm_hcq_bank_cb_rw2 (clk boundary 420.9 ps TT, 349 of 355 sinks). rw4 row-local write assembly (WROW 2: hold / asm / bad per SRAM row on clk_d<r>, clk_a eliminated); stage-control long-reach registers copied per row (STG 1: read enable/address on the row capture root, lane-enable sources + leaf go on clk_e<r>; clk_c = cv/cd chain only); kept beat copies anchored at the xb_v / xb_beat pins so the in-face root clk is pin flops at one face only; rw5m: row read capture + read control folded into clk_d<r> (no clk_w / clk_x). 0 added edges. HBM-COLLECT10/HCQB rw6: the cb_rw5/rw5m gates (ep6, 10-21) FAILED CTS at glue root clk_c: pin-flop spread 104.1 / 102.2 ps TT (263 internal sinks, insertion 641 ps). 3_place sink dump: the cv/cd chain (252 cd + 9 cv + fin_q/f_o) sits at x 8..204 y 7..240 (SW corner, between the d_* in-pins W y130..140 and the o_* out-pins S x130..140) while the clk_c entry was on the E face y 374.7 -> ~700 um trunk. Fix: clk_c entry -> S face x 100..101 (free S segment 0..130, beside the chain). Pin move only; 0 RTL change.",
